\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Easier on Fed's aggressive hike. \b0\par\par\uc2 939 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2000\par 04:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 17 (Reuters) - A widely expected aggressive \par \par \uc2  tightening by the U.S. Federal Reserve overnight pressured most \par \par \uc2  Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar in early Wednesday \par \par \uc2  trade. \par \par \uc2      The Fed raised its key rates by half a percentage point, \par \par \uc2  bringing the federal fund rate for overnight loans between \par \par \uc2  banks  to 6.5 percent and the more symbolic discount rate to \par \par \uc2  six percent. \par \par \uc2      The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded to the move by \par \par \uc2  raising its key overnight rates by a similar half percentage \par \par \uc2  point. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the Philippine peso\tab   opened the day weaker,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dragged down by other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and concerns over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par violence in the southern Mindanao region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Given that growth in these countries (is) still very\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nascent and external risks are increasingly building towards a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slowdown in the U.S. economy...it is very likely that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par governments in these countries will steer towards weaker Asian\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Thio Chin Loo, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at BNP\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Paribas Group in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dollar/yen firmed following the Fed's announcement\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but pared some gains as interbank dealers unwound long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso edged down to a 23-month low despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to raise overnight rates by 50 basis points\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with immediate effect.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A bank official told Reuters the hike would take the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight borrowing rate to 9.5 percent and overnight lending\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to 11.75 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rate hike was on top of the Philippines' move to raise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates by 25 basis points on May 2.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to slide further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on weak regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and worries over violence in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mindanao.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A dealer in Manila said the peso support level stays at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 41.70, adding that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keep it from plunging to 41.80.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab    -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won was slightly softer as players sought to buy the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar after it strengthened against the yen in early trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A foreign bank dealer in Seoul said dollar/won would likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par face resistance at around 1,116 won, where some dollar sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from foreign investors buying local stocks were expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors bought a net 90.23 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shares on the Korea Stock Exchange on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers forecast the won to move between 1,114 and 1,116.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah remained hobbled around 8,600 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par looking set to test recent lows again despite President\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Adurrahman Wahid's call on Tuesday for Bank Indonesia and state\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks to rescue the ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers questioned whether \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bring a sustainable recovery in the rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has already said it does not regard\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or interest rate hikes as a viable solution, as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political factors played a large part in the rupiah's weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said trading in the rupiah would remain thin, as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the confidence crisis grew.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "With all the problems there, no one wants to be short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars, though we could see some (dollar) profit-taking at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 8,650," a dealer at a European bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht edged down in sympathy with other regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and some dealers said it looked set to test the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 39.50 support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar is in favour after the Fed raised borrowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par costs by 50 basis points, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets unless its movements became too volatile.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He also said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would keep a low interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate policy to keep economic recovery on track. The move could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lead to a weaker baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar eased slightly, pressured by a softer yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in early Asian trade. The Sing is managed against a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of which the yen is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par believed to represent a substantial portion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said dollar demand was still strong after the Fed's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decision to raise borrowing costs by a widely-expected 50 basis\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen supported by possible\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore at 1.7350.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It resistance was pegged at 1.7270.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar rebounded on the back of dollar profit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taking after falling to a nearly two-month low on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Players were cautious about pushing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  much lower\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was heard defending it at around T$30.799.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expected Wall Street-inspired gains to help\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par underpin the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  despite some political uncertainties\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of the the presidential inauguration on May 20.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0119 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.53\tab  109.20\tab    -0.30\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7315\tab  1.7293\tab    -0.13\par  Taiwan dlr    30.751\tab  30.782\tab    +0.10\par  Korean won   1115.00\tab 1114.50\tab    -0.04\par  Baht\tab      39.35\tab   39.22\tab    -0.33\par  Peso\tab      41.65\tab   41.62\tab    -0.07\par  Rupiah\tab  8570.00\tab 8500.00\tab    -0.82\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \