\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah down but U.S. rate hike reduces uncertainty. \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2000\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, May 17 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah edged down early on Wednesday on lingering concerns about President Abdurrahman Wahid's handling of the economy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A decision by the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise borrowing costs by 50 basis points, as expected, its biggest move in five years, surprised no one but helped remove one of the negative factors affecting the rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The 50 basis-point hike does help remove one of the negative factors. But concerns remain on the government's poor handling of the economy. Now it no longer has significant external factors to blame," one dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  By 0150 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 8,545/8,595 to the dollar versus 8,500/8,550 in late local trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was traded in a range of between 8,545 to 8,675 rupiah in morning trade and was likely to remain in that range the rest of the day, another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said local corporates were largely on the sidelines, but they were likely to enter the market when the dollar fell below 8,500. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was slow as state banks, which led dollar selling on Tuesday after Wahid asked them to do so, were not yet active in the market in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Wahid on Tuesday asked Bank Indonesia and state banks to help the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which had fallen more than 18 percent against the dollar so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers questioned whether \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could bring a sustainable recovery in the rupiah - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already said it does not regard \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or interest rate hikes as a viable solution as political factors play a large part in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Wahid, facing a growing crisis of confidence in his handling of the economy, also ordered his finance minister to review economic projections in this year's budget which are now looking too optimistic. ((Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5h00dz5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
