\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Shares End Up 3.4% On Tech Rebound,Stronger IDR \b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2000\par 11:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - - 17/05/00 09-07G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0907GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian shares ended higher Wednesday on a technical rebound in blue chips, lifting the main index off a 13-month low reached Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The JSX Composite index ended up 3.4%, or 17.032 points at 514.851. Gainers led decliners 127 to 22, with 41 stocks unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Volume was 375 million shares valued at 729 billion rupiah (IDR). \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at IDR8,395, compared with IDR8,535 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta shares opened higher Wednesday after Wall Street brushed off the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee's 50 basis-point interest rate hike, the head of research at a local brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  He said there was also a sharp increase in the afternoon session after the Indonesian government signed its letter of intent to the International Monetary Fund, which should pave the way for the release of a $400 million loan installment next month. \par \par \uc2  The market was also boosted by a rebound in market heavyweight Telkom after the stock fell IDR200 Tuesday to its lowest level in more than seven months. Telkom ended up IDR225, or 7.6%, at IDR3,175. \par \par \uc2  The head of research at another local brokerage also said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the weakening rupiah helped strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and had a positive effect on the stock market. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin said Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold nearly $300 million to boost the rupiah this week. \par \par \uc2  "People can see now that the government has a strong will to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the head of research said. \par \par \uc2  The research head said a technical rebound across most sectors also helped lift the main index from Tuesday's fall below the key 500 point support level. \par \par \uc2  Blue chips led the recovery, with cigarette stocks regaining lost ground after recent heavy losses. \par \par \uc2  Gudang Garam ended up IDR375, or 3.2%, at IDR12,075, while rival cigarette producer HM Sampoerna added IDR300, or 2.5%, to IDR12,325. \par \par \uc2  International call operator Indosat was also stronger, with its shares closing IDR375 higher, or 3.8%, at IDR10,275. \par \par \uc2  There was also a technical rebound in retail stocks, with Ramayana ending up IDR200, or 4.8%, at IDR4,400, and Matahari adding IDR50, or 5.9%, to IDR900. \par \par \uc2  But automaker Astra International bucked the trend, falling sharply as company employees rushed to offload shares that the company will be grant as options next week. \par \par \uc2  Astra ended down IDR200, or 6.3%, at IDR2,975. \par \par \uc2  The market will be closed Thursday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  -By Leigh Murray 62 21 3983 1277; leigh.murray@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  5055 55109 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5h02ftb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
