\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah off lows on Wahid comments. \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 11:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, May 16 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah was off its lows on Tuesday as dealers covered short rupiah positions after President Abdurrahman Wahid asked Bank Indonesia and state banks to help the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  By 0910 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 8,500/8,550 to the dollar versus a low of 8,725/8,745 in morning trade ahead of Wahid's comments and 8,460/8,510 in late local trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has fallen just over 18 percent so far this year and dealers said if the rupiah strengthens above 8,500, dollar buying will almost certainly return. \par \par \uc2  "Under the law Bank Indonesia is not under the supervision of President Wahid, but still players are worried about being short of rupiah," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers questioned whether \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could bring a sustainable recovery in the rupiah - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already said it does not regard \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or interest rate hikes as a viable solution as political factors play a large part in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Wahid, facing a growing crisis of confidence in his handling of the economy, also ordered his finance minister to review economic projections in this year's budget which are now looking too optimistic. \par \par \uc2  Wahid himself gave a rosy outlook for economic growth this year, saying GDP was expected to grow up to 5.5 percent following two years of deep recession. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian statistics bureau, however, offered a less rosy outlook. On Monday it said growth this year could be as low as 1.54 percent in the worst case, well below previous estimates of around four percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah's rebound on Tuesday was led by state banks. Local corporates, meanwhile, mostly stood to the side. \par \par \uc2  "They are largely on the sidelines waiting for better rates. More corporate dollar buying is likely to emerge when the dollar falls to below 8,500," one said. \par \par \uc2  ((Gde Anugrah Arka, Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5g00i8q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
