\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Ends Almost Flat On Wahid Remarks \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 13:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended almost unchanged Tuesday after President Abdurrahman Wahid called for action to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , arresting the dollar's earlier appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Wahid said he would ask state banks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take action to shore up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in contrast to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments Monday from Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Asian trading at 8,535 rupiah, against IDR8,540 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Wahid's remarks lent some support to the rupiah and prompted some participants to take profit after earlier pushing the dollar to IDR8,740. \par \par \uc2  Wahid also said he had asked the finance minister to look into the impact the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have on the budget. \par \par \uc2  However, the market is still seeking clarity on monetary policy and in particular, how much pressure Wahid is putting on Bank Indonesia to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was made independent last year. \par \par \uc2  Wahid's assertion that the economy could grow up to 5.5% this year also confused the market. His comments came after the Central Statistics Bureau said Monday that the economy would grow by only 1.5% if current conditions persist. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupiah would take its lead Wednesday from the results of the U.S. Federal Reserve's Open Market Committee meeting on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  -By Simon Montlake; 62 21 3983 1277; smontlake@ap.org \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5g02gx4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
