\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Lower Late; Rupiah Off 7-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2000\par 11:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly lower late Tuesday in quiet trade ahead of an expected interest rate hike by the U.S. Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah was slightly weaker, but well above its intraday low. \par \par \uc2  Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and state banks lifted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has plunged as much as 9% over the past week. \par \par \uc2  It rallied sharply from a near seven month-low after Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and state-run banks to support the flagging local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Syetarn Hansakul, an analyst with WestLB, said "Wahid's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comment today helped lend some support but may not be enough if U.S. FOMC (Federal Open Market Committee) impacts negatively tomorrow." \par \par \uc2  It is also unclear if Wahid could order the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which in theory works independently from the president, to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Wahid also instructed Finance Minister Bambang Sudibyo to review the economic projections in this year's budget, which appear too optimistic. The government had based the budget on an exchange rate of 7,000 rupiah to a dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the local session was at 8,545 rupiah, marginally up from IDR8,541 late Monday, but well below its intraday high of IDR8,730. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht, Philippine peso and New Taiwan dollar also drifted lower on expectations of an aggressive U.S. interest rate hike later Tuesday, while the South Korean won bucked the regional downtrend. \par \par \uc2  The FOMC is widely expected to raise short-term interest rates by half a percentage point in an effort to slow rapid U.S. economic growth to a more sustainable rate. \par \par \uc2  As the market has largely factored in a hike of this magnitude, some analysts say they expect a "relief rally" in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short term if this occurs. \par \par \uc2  The extent of the rate hike is expected to be influenced by U.S. inflation data, to be released before the FOMC meets. \par \par \uc2  The looming U.S. rate hike and a domestic political crisis embattling Philippine President Joseph Estrada's administration dragged the Philippine peso to a 19-month low. \par \par \uc2  The Estrada administration has been widely criticized for its handling of the country's hostage crisis. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's gains were, however, capped at 41.640 pesos as banks that were long on dollars opted to take profit at this level before repurchasing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a lower rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at PHP41.630 on the Philippine Dealing System, up from of PHP41.560 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said Tuesday that while the peso should strengthen after jitters over the Fed's rate decision subside, it will likely remain above PHP41 to a dollar in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Buenaventura reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to provide dollar liquidity to the market if necessary, but this hasn't been needed yet. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won ended little changed against the U.S. dollar as afternoon dollar selling by local banks offset earlier dollar buying by overseas players in the non-deliverable forward market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 1,114.60 won, barely changed from Monday's close at KRW1,114.70. \par \par \uc2  Bucking the regional weakness, the Singapore dollar was slightly stronger as participants locked in profits on some long U.S. dollar positions ahead of the FOMC's meeting, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0950 GMT (5:50 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7280, down from S$1.7296 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  A 50 basis-point U.S. rate increase will be neutral for the Singapore dollar, traders said, adding that they expected the U.S. unit to continue trading in a range of between S$1.7250 and S$1.7350. \par \par \uc2  However, the outlook for the likely level of the Singapore dollar has been clouded by the expectation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, the de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the upper end of that range. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail; 65-421-4807 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5g02gjq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
