\par\par \b \uc2  Battered rupiah cuts losses on Wahid comments. \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, May 12 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah fell further on Friday on growing pessimism about the economy, but managed to claw back some ground late in the day after President Abdurrahman Wahid said the government may act to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah dived to a new seven-month low of 8,750 to the dollar during the day but was quoted at 8,460/8,510 by 0850 GMT, compared with 8,390/8,420 in late local trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  There was market talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but dealers said there was little Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could do to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if such a move was considered effective. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah cut its losses after Wahid said the government would take action to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it did not rebound by Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Wahid's comments prompted profit-taking (in the dollar) as the comments raised fresh fears the government might be tempted to apply a fixed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate regime, even though the possibility seems to be remote," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said she wondered what the government, in particular Wahid, had in mind to boost the rupiah. She cautioned that if Wahid did nothing to prop up the rupiah, the inaction would badly hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The president has taken over supervision of economic matters after the IMF delayed a loan disbursement due to slow progress on the economic front. \par \par \uc2  There have been worries about possible friction between the President and his economic czar, but Wahid again denied this on Friday saying his relations with the minister were still good. \par \par \uc2  Wahid said the rupiah's falls were due partly to fears of unrest to mark the second anniversary of riots in Jakarta on May 13 and 14, 1998. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the weakness was more due to growing pessimism about the government's competence to turn the economy around. \par \par \uc2  They said the rupiah's falls were the result of an accummulation of disappointments over Wahid's handling of economic and political affairs. \par \par \uc2  Wahid's recent comment that an unidentified group was trying to topple him also rattled markets this week, dealers said. ((Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5c00mur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
