\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Shares End Down As Rupiah Weakens Further \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 11:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Indonesian shares ended lower Friday on fears the rupiah could weaken further and after Bank Indonesia warned of a possible interest rate hike. \par \par \uc2  The JSX Composite index ended down 0.4%, or 2.324 points at 526.877. Decliners led gainers 55 to 46, with 94 stocks unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Volume was 233 million shares valued at 494 billion rupiah (IDR). \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at IDR8,475, compared with IDR8,393 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A local dealer said many investors avoided the market due to the weakening rupiah, which touched a low of IDR8,775 against the greenback Friday - its lowest level since Sept. 23. \par \par \uc2  She said further rupiah instability could push the main index down to 500 points next week. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer with a foreign brokerage said market sentiment was further damped by comments by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin, who said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading only if it will be effective in boosting the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  His comment was interpreted by the market as a refusal by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the market was also concerned of a possible increase in domestic interest rates, which Sjahril said Bank Indonesia would do if the U.S. Federal Reserve raises the Federal fund rate by more than 50 basis points next week. \par \par \uc2  Blue chips were hardest hit by the rupiah's weakness, with market heavyweight Telkom losing IDR50, or 1.5%, to IDR3,275. \par \par \uc2  Cigarette producer Gudang Garam ended down IDR75, or 0.6%, at IDR12,500, while rival HM Sampoerna fell IDR50, or 0.4%, to IDR12,975. \par \par \uc2  International call operator Indosat was also hit - its shares ended down IDR100, or 0.9%, at IDR10,500. \par \par \uc2  But oil producer Medco Energi Corp. bucked the trend, with its shares ending up IDR125, or 3%, to IDR4,250 as the stronger dollar led to buying. All of Medco's profits are in U.S dollars. \par \par \uc2  -By Leigh Murray 62 21 3983 1277; leigh.murray@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  5055 55109 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5c02crl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
