\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Wahid: IDR Weaker Due To May Riots Anniversary \b0\par\par\uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 09:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The current weakness of the rupiah is due to concerns about demonstrations to mark the second anniversary of the riots that shook Jakarta in May 1998, President Abdurrahman Wahid said Friday. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters at his residence, Wahid said that "businessmen are buying dollars, because of concerns about the anniversary of the May riots," which is weighing on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  He said the government would take action next week to shore up the rupiah - after the riots' anniversary - if necessary, although he didn't say what kind of action. \par \par \uc2  "We will wait until May 15," he said. "If the dollar doesn't weaken, then the government will take action." \par \par \uc2  Several groups of protestors are gathering in Jakarta, some to mark the anniversary of the killing of four students by police at Trisakti University in western Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  The four, who died May 12, 1998, were part of a massive swell of student-led protests and riots that year, which led to the downfall of former President Suharto on May 21. \par \par \uc2  Earlier Friday, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if the move will be effective in boosting the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  "I cannot say at what level we will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he told journalists. "We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if we think it will be effective." \par \par \uc2  Sjahril added that Bank Indonesia won't guide up local interest rates if the U.S. Federal Reserve raises the Federal funds rate by only 0.50 percentage point. \par \par \uc2  "We will follow suit only if the Fed raises interest rates above 0.50 percentage point," Sjahril said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the rupiah's slump to expectations of a 50-basis point increase in U.S. interest rates next week, combined with the general demand for dollars from local companies and domestic political uncertainties. \par \par \uc2  At 0739 GMT (3:39 a.m. EDT), the dollar was trading at IDR8,703, up from IDR8,393 late Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is off its session highs, but still is at its highest level since Sept. 23. \par \par \uc2  Wahid also said he won't sack Senior Economics Minister Kwik Kian Gie for remarks that Indonesia was too unstable for foreign investors. Wahid's comments helped quash speculation that such a move was imminent. \par \par \uc2  "I have no plans to replace Kwik Kian Gie," Wahid told reporters. "I have a very good relationship with him." \par \par \uc2  The president's expression of support comes after Kwik said that Indonesia isn't stable enough to attract foreign investors, comments that fueled a perception that the minister would be fired. \par \par \uc2  In a wide-ranging interview with Dow Jones Newswires Thursday, Kwik said the country still faced too much instability, sporadic anarchy, and social unrest to appeal to investors. \par \par \uc2  "I never talk about foreign investment and things like that because I'm realistic enough: if I were a foreign investor, I wouldn't come to Indonesia," he said. "The law enforcement is not there, but not only that, the whole thing is so confusing. How can you come here?" \par \par \uc2  But Kwik later played down the comments, saying he wasn't actually asking investors to avoid investing in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  -By Leigh Murray 62 21 3983 1277; leigh.murray@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5c02cg5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
