\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Wahid Offers No Quick Solution To Boost Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 06:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Indonesian President Abdurrahman Wahid offered no quick solutions Friday on how to arrest the rupiah's slide against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "I think we should wait for a week," Wahid told a press conference. "We shouldn't rush to make any comment because there was no unexpected thing happening domestically" which caused the rupiah to weaken. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the rupiah continued its slide to levels not seen since early October 1999. At 0454 GMT (12:54 a.m. EDT), the dollar was trading at 8,555 rupiah, up from its close at IDR8,390 late Thursday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite repeated statements by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials that it would do so to boost the embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana; 62 21 3983 1277; imsentana@ap.org \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw5c02c7s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
