\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah breaks 8,100/dlr on US rates, local nerves. \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2000\par 04:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, May 10 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah fell through 8,100 for the first time since mid-October in early trade on Wednesday, hit by the prospect of higher U.S. rates and concerns over the country's political stability and economic progress. \par \par \uc2  By 0130 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 8,155/8,175 against the dollar compared with 8,060/8,080 in late local trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Weak regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to speculation about higher U.S. interest rates dampened sentiment in the rupiah. The fears have prompted players to buy dollars now to repay or refinance foreign debt," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Another bank dealer said most of the dollar buying orders in morning trading came from interbank players. He said local corporates were likely to follow suit later on Wednesday which could put further pressure on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  There were no signs yet of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up the rupiah, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to do so if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved closer to 8,200, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said the rupiah's fall to a low of 8,135 in New York trade overnight hurt sentiment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asian morning trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A string of recent discouraging news on the domestic front also hit sentiment in the rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  President Abdurrahman Wahid said on Monday a "certain group" was trying to topple him before the upcoming meeting of Indonesia's highest legislative body in August. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the government's slow progress in bank and corporate restructuring continued to dampen sentiment on the rupiah. ((Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5a00ttw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
