\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah up ahead of president-parliament meeting. \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2000\par 04:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 27 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah inched up early on Thursday as players sold dollars to take profits after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell through 8,000 to six-month lows on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Market sentiment, however, remained cautious as the market was awaiting President Abdurrahman Wahid's appearance before parliament later today where he will be quizzed on several controversial issues, including his plans to revoke a ban on communism. \par \par \uc2  By 0145 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 7,970/8,000 to the dollar compared with 8,020/8,050 in late local trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer said immediate support for the rupiah was seen at 8,075 while resistance seen at 7,925. \par \par \uc2  "Most of those taking profits are interbank players. Players are now waiting for the outcome of the meeting between President Wahid and parliamentary members," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Monday's sacking of Investment and State Enterprises Minister Laksamana Sukardi and Trade Minister Yusuf Kalla is not on the agenda, but Wahid has been widely criticised over the move and it may well be raised during the meeting. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said oral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to be effective this time. Players sold dollars to take profit after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the market to prop up the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah broke through 8,000 to the dollar on Wednesday, hit by doubts over the government's unity and economic competence following the sacking of two cabinet ministers earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The sacking of the two ministers has sparked fears their parties could pull out of Indonesia ramshackle coalition and doubts over the ability of their replacements. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's auction of one-month SBI certificates resulted in a weighted average interest rate of 10.88 percent, down from 10.92 percent last week. ((Gde Anugrah Arka, Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4r01jj2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
