\par\par \b \uc2  Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  says no need for rph  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2000\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 26 (Reuters) - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin said on Wednesday there was no need at present to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "if it was necessary". \par \par \uc2  Sabirin told reporters he did not expect the rupiah's current weakness to last long, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could strengthen to 7,000 to the dollar if there were no serious political upheavals in the country. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would raise interest rates to defend the rupiah, he said: "At this moment, no." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell through 8,000 to the dollar on Wednesday for the first time since October on concerns about a potential rift in the government after the sacking of two economics ministers earlier this week. ((Muklis Ali, Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4q01kty\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
