\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah loses further ground after breaking 8,000. \b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2000\par 05:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 26 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah lost further ground early on Wednesday after falling through 8,000 to the dollar for the first time since the mid-October as the sacking of two ministers raised concerns over rifts in the government. \par \par \uc2  By 0240 GMT the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 8,040/8,060 against the dollar compared with 7,930/7,940 in late local trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Our strategy is to remain long on dollars because of the political uncertainty. I see immediate support for the rupiah at 8,100 and resistance for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 7,950," one European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the market was already long on dollars but there were many players who were nervous because of rising political uncertainty. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there were no signs yet that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin said on Wednesday there was no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the rupiah, saying the local unit could reach 7,000 to the dollar if there was no further political upheaval. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah had moved closer to 8,000 late last week but failed to break through the barrier due in part to support from local players, believed to be acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Monday night, President Abdurrahman Wahid fired Investment and State Enterprises Minister Laksamana Sukardi and Trade Minister Yusuf Kalla, saying the country needed a united cabinet to deal with the battered economy. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said doubts surrounded Laksamana's replacement by a subordinate whose main qualification seems to be his closeness to Wahid. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say fighting among political parties for control of lucrative positions in government, state companies and the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA) has hampered policy. The state enterprises ministry is seen as a key money spinner for the party that controls it. \par \par \uc2  The sackings came at the start of an IMF review into how closely Indonesia is sticking to its agreement on economic reforms in return for a $400 million loan payment, as well as substantial Paris Club debt rescheduling. \par \par \uc2  Acting IMF head Stanley Fischer said on Monday he hoped the delayed loan payment would finally be released by the end of May. It had originally been scheduled for early April but was put on hold because of government foot-dragging on implementing planned reforms. ((Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw4q01ctc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
