\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Sick yen unnerves baht, Taiwan dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 943 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2000\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Firmness in dollar/yen gnawed \par \par \uc2  at regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Tuesday, with the Thai baht \par \par \uc2  leading the losers after shedding some 0.4 percent. \par \par \uc2      Only the Singapore dollar managed to tip-toe into positive \par \par \uc2  terrain following a slight bout of U.S. dollar profit-taking. \par \par \uc2      Options-related dollar sales triggered ahead of 112 yen \par \par \uc2   elbowed dollar/yen off six-month highs of 111.73 but yen \par \par \uc2  sentiment remained weak on worries over Japan's growth \par \par \uc2  prospects. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Economic Planning Minister Taichi Sakaiya said \par \par \uc2  recent yen levels of around 111 to the dollar were appropriate \par \par \uc2  for Japanese corporates' profits as well as for exporters. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   gained against both the yen and the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as yen carry trades were revisited and after Moody's Investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Service put Japan's yen-denominated debt rating on review for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible downgrade last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Players took advantage of a negative stock market to unload\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht, pushing the unit to its lowest level in two months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the market was also happy to push the baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  described its fall last week as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par driven by normal market forces.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We should be running into a wall of resistance at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 38.35 to 38.50 area," said a dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar looked set to strengthen against the baht for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rest of the week, but dealers expected the baht to remain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par well supported in the medium term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The Thai baht in the medium term should strengthen back to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 37.70 to 37.50 area, maybe within the next couple of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months," a dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The weaker yen and jitters after China demanded the island\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par enter peace talks or face attack unnerved the Taiwan dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forcing it to close around nine local cents lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     China's ultimatum comes as Taiwan prepares for a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par presidential election in March which hinges on the state of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan-China ties.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taipei dealers said this forced investors to reload U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions while falls on the stock market also lent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar support as some institutional investors repatriated\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profits.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON\tab     -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Speculative offshore dollar buying in the light of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/yen's rise and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the monetary authorities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forced the won to end lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Seoul dealers said offshore players bought around $200\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million during the day and they detected purchases of an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par estimated $50 million by state-run banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea said seasonally adjusted unemployment fell to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 4.6 percent in January, its lowest level since January 1998\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par when it was 4.2 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Kim Dae-Jung said in an Italian newspaper\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interview he would work to keep inflation and interest rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par under 10 percent by keeping a tight check on money supply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was again range trading with little activity in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market, though dealers cited some onshore selling interest.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There may be quite a number of Indonesian banks that need\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to roll over non-performing loans (NPL's), which are attracting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some interest from some Singapore quarters looking to take over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some of the loans," said a dealer at a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "If that were to fall through, then naturally, there would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be (more) dollar demand," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     There was dollar selling interest at the 7,440 level with a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further barrier seen at 7,500.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may want to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 7,500 level to prevent the rupiah weakening too fast, though\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one said 7,500 would still be within range for this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Profit-taking after the dollar's substantial gains in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent days barely lifted the Sing dollar into positive\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par territory, with dealers eyeing the direction of dollar/yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said further losses in the Straits Times index\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had not had much impact as Sing movements had been more closely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par correlated with the weakening yen of late.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dollar/Sing was likely to remain well bid, especially if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar poked above 112 yen and beyond, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Strong dollar support was seen at 1.7010, a low hit on Feb\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 17. Most analysts still stuck to average expectations for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing to hit around 1.59 per dollar by year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was tracking other regionals throughout the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with very thin volumes and a narrow range, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think it should not cross 41 at this point, but if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further tension from the China/Taiwan issue spreads through the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par region, then the herd mentality may take the dollar up against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par all the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said an analyst at a European\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par house.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0915 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2