\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Market Rates Steady On Ample Liquidity \b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 1999\par 03:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Indonesian money market rates are mostly steady early Friday as most banks have ample liquidity on hand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0138 GMT (8:38 p.m. Thursday EST), the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was between 11% and 11.5% for local banks, steady from Thursday's level of around 11%, dealers said. The rate for most foreign and joint venture banks was between 10.75% and 11%, little changed from around 10.5% Thursday, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said liquidity remains ample as Bank Indonesia released 3.341 trillion rupiah into the system earlier in the day as funds it absorbed in previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  matured. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily to manage liquidity in the system. \par \par \uc2  "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps liquidity ample as it wants to prevent interest rates from increasing from their current levels," a dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the dollar was trading at IDR7,240, up slightly from IDR7,230 late Thursday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana; 62 21 3983 1277; imsentana@ap.org \par \par \uc2  1185 4281 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvca08gaq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
