\par\par \b \uc2  Official Cites Web Of Corruption In Bank Negara Indonesia Lending \b0\par\par\uc2 950 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 15:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Indonesia -(Dow Jones)- Indonesia's scandal-ridden banking sector was stung by fresh revelations of corruption Monday, this time by an allegation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and former President Suharto were involved in a conspiracy related to the handling of 9.65 trillion rupiah ($1.34 billion) in loans to the Texmaco Group, an influential conglomerate. \par \par \uc2  Laksamana Sukardi, the government's minister of investment and state enterprises, told Parliament that loans by PT Bank Negara Indonesia to the Texmaco Group involved "a ... high-level conspiracy." \par \par \uc2  The alleged conspiracy dated to late 1997, following the crash of Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupiah, a tumble that impaired the financial positions of most Indonesian conglomerates. \par \par \uc2  Laksamana revealed that Bank Indonesia - the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - provided a total of $754.1 million plus 1.9 trillion rupiah in a preshipment trade-financing package to the Texmaco Group, contravening \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations that allowed only postshipment loans. \par \par \uc2  The group faced increasing financial strain as the rupiah depreciated, and had about $350 million in matured commercial paper and Yankee bonds that couldn't be rolled over. \par \par \uc2  Suharto \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by instructing Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in writing to extend the facility and flout its own rules, Laksamana said, adding that the "preshipment facility was tailor-made for Texmaco and is a case of national-level collusion." \par \par \uc2  The Texmaco Group is controlled by Manimaren Sinivasan, who, according to the state-enterprises minister, is a close friend of Suharto. Manimaren's brother, Marimutu Manimaren, is a treasurer for former ruling party Golkar, and was named in the PricewaterhouseCoopers audit of the PT Bank Bali case. The Bank Bali scandal contributed to the downfall of B.J. Habibie, Suharto's successor. as president. \par \par \uc2  Further, Laksamana said Bank Indonesia tapped into the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to provide the Texmaco Group with the loans, at a time when the rupiah faced heavy devaluation pressures. "Bank Indonesia used the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to bail out a local company at a time when Indonesia (was) in dire need of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  The amount of credit channeled through Bank Negara to Texmaco breached lending limits prescribed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which stipulate that no bank can lend more than 20% of its capital to a single borrower, he said, without quantifying the percentage involved. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  waived this rule to allow the loans to the Texmaco Group. \par \par \uc2  Laksamana added that Suharto's interference in Bank Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  was clear. \par \par \uc2  Even the ministry of trade and industry at that time turned a blind eye to the fact that only the Texmaco Group received preshipment loans, although the ministry had recommended two other business groups for such assistance. \par \par \uc2  The alleged collusion didn't stop after the loans were granted. A local media report disclosed and Bank Negara subsequently confirmed that it didn't report its loan exposure to the Texmaco Group to the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency, or IBRA, which was formed last year to reform the banking sector. Bank Negara is among the banks tagged for government recapitalization, to the tune of 52.8 trillion rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Under the recapitalization program, Bank Negara should have transferred the worst of its nonperforming loans to IBRA for recovery, since IBRA is empowered to tackle recalcitrant debtors. \par \par \uc2  Despite the Texmaco Group's failure to repay any of the loans that led Bank Negara to write off the debts completely last year, the bank didn't transfer the loans to IBRA. Most banking analysts say such loans should have been transferred to IBRA for more effective collection. \par \par \uc2  Pradjoto, a banking analyst who blew the whistle on the Bank Bali matter, said a big question is why Bank Negara didn't transfer the loans to IBRA. He suggested that the bank "is trying to avoid letting the powerful IBRA to be Texmaco's creditor." \par \par \uc2  If the loans were transferred, the Texmaco Group probably would be at or near the top of the list of IBRA's debtors in terms of the amount owed. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara, which isn't related to Bank Negara, Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said earlier Monday that it is negotiating with the Texmaco Group on a debt-restructuring plan that would include a debt-to-equity conversion for part of the debt. \par \par \uc2  The bank's secretary, Sudirman, who like many Indonesians uses a single name, said the bank doesn't view the loans to the Texmaco Group as being so dire as to qualify for government recapitalization. The bank said the loans were classified as Category 4, meaning they were considered more likely to be repaid. In March, Bank Negara passed on the IBRA loans totaling 24.3 trillion rupiah. Those loans were rated as Category 5, meaning there was a very low chance of recovery. \par \par \uc2  Sudirman said Germany's Commerzbank AG is advising on the loan restructuring, but added that it is premature to state which of the Texmaco Group companies would be turned over to the bank. \par \par \uc2  The daily newspaper Harian Ekonomi Neraca said Monday that bank would gain control of five group companies and would seek a U.S. stock market listing for three of the units: PT Texmaco Perkasa Engineering, PT Perkasa Heavyndo Engineering and PT Multikarsa Investama. Of the three, only Texmaco Perkasa Engineering, which makes heavy equipment, is listed in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Multikarsa Investama has 4.08 trillion rupish of the total loan to the group, according to a statement released Friday by the Jakarta Stock Exchange. The second-largest debtor is the group's Polysindo Eka Perkasa unit with 1.45 trillion rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020330dvbt00kjl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
