\par\par \b \uc2  Thai c.bank watching baht, no reason to worry-PM. \b0\par\par\uc2 192 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Thai Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai told reporters on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was closely watching the movement of the baht and there was no reason to worry about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The baht at current levels is in line with expectations of most economists, who say that the baht at 36-40 to the dollar is not a cause of concern," Chuan said. \par \par \uc2  Chuan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  decline was in line with those of other regional units in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chuan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was monitoring the situation. \par \par \uc2  Chuan said that although the weaker baht had caused a hike in domestic oil prices, it would benefit Thai exporters. \par \par \uc2  The baht remained at its lowest level since September 23 in early morning trade. It was trading at 40.05/40.10 to the doller against 40.00/40.05 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  ((Kettiya Jittapong, Bangkok Newsroom +66-2 637 5500 ext 418 \par \par \uc2  email:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9h00f08\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
