\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Indonesia/Rupiah -2: East Timor Weighs On IDR \b0\par\par\uc2 139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1999\par 09:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to help support the sliding rupiah, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters ahead of a parliamentary hearing on the Bank Bali scandal, Sjahril said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  now wouldn't be really useful, given the current market sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "Given the current pressure in the market, we're not going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Sjahril said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now awaiting the settlement of the non-economic events that affect the rupiah sentiment," he said, referring to the chaos in East Timor. \par \par \uc2  He added the East Timor crisis - rather than the scandal linked to the disappearance of funds from the nationalized PT Bank Bali - was weighing on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0701GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9806js6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
