\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Colombia peso at new depths. \b0\par\par\uc2 970 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1999\par 11:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 8 (Reuters) - Colombia's crawling-peg \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system was looking shaky on Wednesday after the peso hit an all-time closing low against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were dented again by Indonesia, where carnage in East Timor and a scandal at Bank Bali forced the rupiah through 8,500 to the dollar despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty sank deeper into the weak side of its broad trading band after a downward revision in the official growth forecast, and on continued concern that some privatisation inflows will be kept out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that Colombia will be forced to scrap its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system and float the peso has escalated since Chile decided last week to do away with its own trading bands. \par \par \uc2  The Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped a further 1.2 percent on Tuesday to a record closing low of 1,981.5 to the dollar in Bogota, just 4.15 pesos above the floor of its daily band. \par \par \uc2  It was unmoved during the London morning, which generally sees very little Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, but was expected to come under further pressure later in the day. \par \par \uc2  Colombia needs to cut interest rates to stimulate the recession-hit economy, and analysts say it is only a matter of time before it ditches the band. \par \par \uc2  "If they have a further testing of the band and the markets know the political willpower is not there to raise interest rates, that could be the breaking point," said Neil Dougall, Latin America economist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in London. \par \par \uc2  RUPIAH DIVES \par \par \uc2  The rupiah dived further amid fears the East Timor violence could affect much-needed loans from donors as the international community presses Indonesia to clamp down on anti-independence militias sowing terror in the territory. \par \par \uc2  The Bank Bali scandal also continued to rumble, with preliminary results from a probe into alleged insider trading due to be presented to parliament next week. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Syahril Sabirin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah, but the action was having little effect. The government target for the rupiah was still in the range of 6,000 to 7,000 to the dollar, he added. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's slide and this week's weaker yen tone continued to take their toll on other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht dropped through 39 to the dollar on Tuesday, hitting an 11-month low of 39.40, and remained firmly on the weaker side of 39 on Wednesday. The Philippine peso also fell sharply, tumbling through 40 to the dollar to 10-month lows. \par \par \uc2  UNCERTAINTY INCREASES \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Indonesia's woes were an excuse to sell Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as uncertainty increased ahead of the year-end. \par \par \uc2  "There's no reason to think that what goes on in East Timor will affect the economies of Thailand or the Philippines, or to a certain extent even Singapore," Andrew Dermot-Fung, economist at Standard Chartered in Singapore, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "But in this kind of environment, with the Y2K issue, investments are just not really flowing into East Asia. Everyone wants to wait and see what's going to happen...(and) any excuse will be taken to sell off the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The zloty, which fell below its basket parity on Tuesday for the first time since March, weakened further to around 0.90 percent below the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  A revision of the Finance Ministry's GDP growth forecast to 5.2 percent from 5.6 percent in 2000 added to gloom over reduced prospects for capital flows into the market. \par \par \uc2  But most analysts said the zloty selloff was overdone, as a suggested debt buyback would use up only a small proportion of the large privatisation inflows expected later this year. \par \par \uc2  ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, \par \par \uc2  including the change versus late New York trade the previous day \par \par \uc2  and the change in the year to date. \par \par \uc2  ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly \par \par \uc2  quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to \par \par \uc2  reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted \par \par \uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in \par \par \uc2  units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the \par \par \uc2  rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. \par \par \uc2  ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the \par \par \uc2  first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.71   36.61    0.28%   5.48%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.34    4.35   -0.09%   6.69%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 254.59  254.99   -0.16%   1.35%\par Slovakia\tab \tab 