\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah touches 8,500 to dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1999\par 09:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah fell to 8,500 to the dollar on Wednesday amid concerns about the crisis in troubled East Timor. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah recovered slightly a few minutes later and was trading at 8,440/8,490 at around 0618 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah broke the 8,500 level when most Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were having lunch. A player from Singapore bought a dollar offer at 8,500 probably from Indonesian players," a dealer with a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was below 8,500 was on April 27. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected further losses in the rupiah after overseas markets open. \par \par \uc2  Players took profits at around midday which brought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the 8,300 level against the dollar but then it weakened again because sentiment was very weak, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said investors were concerned about international pressure on Indonesia's government due to the East Timor chaos and other domestic worries including the unresolved Bank Bali  scandal. \par \par \uc2  The IMF's statements that it is worried about Jakarta's economic program, the scandal over PT Bank Bali Tbk and the situation in East Timor caused players to release their rupiah holdings, dealers said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the sliding rupiah was having little impact. \par \par \uc2  The IMF said on Tuesday it is reviewing the situation in Indonesia and will shortly make a decision on whether to send a mission to Jakarta that was previously scheduled for mid-September. Bank Indonesia also said on Wednesday it would hold interest rates at current levels in the near future due to political and economic uncertainties. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia is due to hold its regular auction of one and three month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  SBI certificates on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the possible further decline in the SBI rates would make the rupiah even less attractive. ((Moris Morissan, Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9800wic\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
