\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah weakens on bank controversy. \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1999\par 12:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah weakened on Monday as investors remained cautious about a bank scandal which kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under selling pressure. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 0924 GMT the rupiah\tab   was quoted at 7,530/7,585 against the dollar compared with 7,580/7,610 in early trade. It ended local trade on Friday at 7,350/7,450.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah weakened as players wait for an overall solution over the bank controversy," one dealer with a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer expected the rupiah to be traded in the range of 7,600/7,800 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The market was still very nervous about PT Bank Bali Tbk  and there seem to be few reasons to go long of rupiah while the situation remains so unclear, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of state banks coming in early to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  A row over a large payment made by Bank Bali to have loans recovered from the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA) has hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets, undermined confidence in IBRA and prompted Golkar dissidents to warn the party may drop Habibie as its presidential candidate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to talk up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and is selling around $5-10 million a day, although it insists this does not represent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But despite Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts, the rupiah has remained vulnerable. \par \par \uc2  "Until you get a clearer situation on what is going to happen with the banks and who is going to be blamed, the rupiah looks less attractive," a local dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the parliamentary faction of the ruling Golkar party said Finance Minister Bambang Subianto and IBRA chief Glenn Yusuf should step down because of the controversy. ((Moris Morissan, Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8n021pr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
