\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah slides as nerves shake foreign players. \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1999\par 05:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah retreated under fresh offshore selling pressure on Monday as nervousness about a mounting bank scandal kept the screws on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  By 0230 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 7,580/7,610 after early offshore dollar buying dragged it through 7,500. It ended local trade on Friday at 7,350/7,450. \par \par \uc2  "There has been little news over the weekend but the market is still very nervous about Bank Bali and there seem to be few reasons to go long of rupiah while the situation remains so unclear," said a dealer at a European bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of state banks coming in early to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  A row over a large payment made by Bank Bali  to have loans recovered from the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA) has hurt the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets, undermined confidence in IBRA and prompted Golkar dissidents to warn the party may drop Habibie as its presidential candidate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to talk up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and is selling around $5-10 million a day, although it insists this does not represent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But despite Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts, the rupiah has remained vulnerable. \par \par \uc2  "Until you get a clearer situation on what is going to happen with the banks and who is going to be blamed, the rupiah looks less attractive," a local dealer said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the parliamentary faction of the ruling Golkar party said Finance Minister Bambang Subianto and IBRA chief Glenn Yusuf should step down because of the controversy. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade was thin, with most of the early action taking place offshore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market had already discounted an expected U.S. interest rate hike this week, and attention would be focused more on Indonesian interest rates. The benchmark one-month SBI rate will be set at an auction on Wednesday. ((Andrew Marshall, Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384 6364, Fax +62 21 344 8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8n020ze\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
