\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Money Rates Open Flat; Rates Seen Heading Down \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 1999\par 04:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's money market rates opened flat Monday morning on an ample money supply, but dealers said rates may head down in the afternoon as some banks appeared to be caught holding too much liquidity. \par \par \uc2  At 0240 GMT (10:06 p.m. EDT Sunday), the interbank overnight rate - considered the benchmark rate - was between 12.0% and 12.5%, unchanged from late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the new clearing system for interbank transactions, which was supposed to be implemented Monday, was delayed. In the past few trading session, banks have been lending very conservatively in anticipation of the new clearing system. \par \par \uc2  "Now the system will be delayed until further notice by Bank Indonesia, some banks may end up having too much liquidity," said a dealer with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The precautions were taken in case the new system, which allows same day settlement of interbank transactions, has any glitches in its initial implementation. \par \par \uc2  The current clearing system is T+1, meaning that it takes one day to settle an interbank trade. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily in the market to absorb excess liquidity and has maintained its overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate steady at 11.75% - the level maintained since the beginning of last week. \par \par \uc2  The market normally trades at 25 basis points to 50 basis points above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  At 0241 GMT (10:41 p.m. EDT Sunday) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the rupiah was quoted at IDR7,760 to the dollar, stronger than the IDR7,900 traded late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; 6221-3983-1277; nfung@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0250GMT \par \par \uc2  1185 4281 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8g061o3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
