\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Market Rates Flat In Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 1999\par 04:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money-market rates were mostly steady early Monday as trading was thin on a lack of fresh news, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said most banks have enough liquidity to cover their needs, so most stayed clear of the market. \par \par \uc2  At 0215 GMT (10:15 p.m. Sunday EDT), the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was unchanged between 12% and 12.5% \par \par \uc2  "Some local banks offered rupiah funds at higher rates than the rates on Friday, but they cut it back as no banks took their offer," a dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier cut its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate for periods between two and four days by 25 basis points, to 12.25%. Dealers viewed the cut as a simple adjustment to bring the rate in line with those on other periods, which were cut last week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the overnight rate at 11.72% and the one-week rate at 12.5%. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at 0215 GMT, the dollar was trading at 7,020 rupiah, up slightly from IDR7,010 late Friday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana; (62-21) 3983 1277; imsentana@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0241GMT \par \par \uc2  1185 4281 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8905tkk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
