\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Indonesia Continues To Push Interest Rates Down \b0\par\par\uc2 764 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1999\par 13:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  By Grainne McCarthy \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--After running into some resistance to allowing interest rates to fall, Bank Indonesia has managed to convince \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets that the decline can continue without harming the rupiah, market participants say. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say that by regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money markets, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has managed to signal that interest rates should continue to fall, without causing the rupiah to slip. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is winning the battle against market sentiment," said Pardi Kendy, head of treasury at PT Bank Buana. "It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the exchange rate below 7,000 (to the dollar) and it's managed to switch sentiment towards the rupiah back to neutral." \par \par \uc2  Short-term Sertificat Bank Indonesia interest rates have tumbled from around 35% at the beginning of the year to 13.13% at the weekly auction Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The rate decline, which has been gradual and steady, has happened over the past few months largely without damaging the rupiah. This has been due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's successful efforts to decouple the exchange rate from interest rates. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, however, the decline in interest rates caused some jitters in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, prompting participants to sell rupiah, believing that the low rates render it unattractive to hold. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This led to a slip in the rupiah to around IDR7,000 to the dollar from\par around IDR6,800 and raised concerns that the rupiah's long bull run had\par ended.\par -\par               \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Pushes Neutral Stance\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, market watchers say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has managed to convince\par the market to adopt a more neutral stance toward the rupiah by using\par state banks to aggressively sell dollars for rupiah and heave market\par sentiment around. The fact that the pace of the interest rate decline\par has slowed also has helped to limit any market panic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There are a lot of psychological factors involved in trading rupiah,\par when somebody buys or sells in a big way, everybody follows suit," said\par a dealer at Citibank in Jakarta.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "When state banks sell dollars aggressively like they have been doing,\par this eliminates the panic effect and people start to ask whether it's\par really worth it to buy dollars at these levels," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although Bank Indonesia doesn't unilaterally decide how much rates\par should fall by - the market does - the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can greatly\par influence the direction of yields by its presence in the market and by\par guiding rates down.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders note that while the rupiah hasn't strengthened over recent\par weeks due to a lack of major supporting factors, it hasn't really\par weakened either. Repeated comments from government and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par officials indicating they're satisfied with the current rupiah level\par have also helped to stop the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from slipping.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah late Wednesday was quoted at IDR6,915, slightly lower than\par IDR6,865 late Tuesday in Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the money markets, Bank Indonesia has helped guide rates close to\par all-time lows while maintaining ample liquidity in the market, dealers\par say.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "By edging down the overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate gradually, Bank\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sends a psychological message to the market," said a money\par market dealer at a U.S. bank in Jakarta.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This indicates rates are going to come down again and limits market\par concerns about sudden interest rate declines," the dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has been steadily cutting its overnight\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate over recent months, Tuesday cut the rate at which it\par offers to absorb liquidity from the market to 11.75% from 12% and\par maintained that rate Wednesday ahead of the SBI rate cut.\par -\par                 Interest Rate Declines Crucial\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Pushing down interest rates has been a major focus of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Under advice from the International Monetary Fund, interest rates\par were jacked up last year at the height of Indonesia's financial crisis\par to help prop up the then-plummeting rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The high rates - which rocketed to around 70% at one point -had a\par drastic effect on much of Indonesia's real economy and its banks.\par Lowering the rates is viewed as crucial to kickstarting the economy\par again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With inflation falling at a rapid pace, economists reckon Bank\par Indonesia can continue to guide interest rates lower, although whether\par they can fall to historic single-digit lows is viewed as unlikely.\par (Indonesian interest rates have never been in single digits, the lowest\par pre-crisis level was around 11.75% in 1987.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Grainne McCarthy; 6221 3983 1277; gmccarthy@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-08-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1148GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1141 4203 55126 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8405toz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
