\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah paces within tight range. \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1999\par 12:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 27 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah was steady in tight range-bound trade on Tuesday, with offshore players putting pressure on the dollar whenever trading moved closer to the 7,000 resistance level. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 6,960/6,970 against the dollar in late local trade on Tuesday compared with 6,995/7,015 in late trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Trading remains mostly in a very tight range. Players are take profit whenever trading moves closer to around 7,000," one foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said firmer regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped boost sentiment on the rupiah despite a further plunge on the local stock market, which lost 3.3 percent at the close on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Firmer regionals helped boost the rupiah despite a further plunge on the stock market today," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was also likely to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help prop up the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Upbeat economic forecasts by chief economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin did not have much impact on the market as the comments had largely been expected, they said. \par \par \uc2  Ginanjar told international donors in Paris GDP growth in the fiscal year to March 31 was seen at 1.5-2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  In Jakarta, Sabirin said month-on-month inflation in July was likely to be negative. He also said there was room for a further interest rate fall this week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said political issues remained among a focus after the election commission on Monday failed to endorse the results of the June 7 parliamentary election. \par \par \uc2  President B.J. Habibie on Monday gave Indonesia's official election monitor one week to check complaints about the poll. \par \par \uc2  ((Jakarta newsroom +62 21 384-6364; Fax +6221 344-8404, jakarta.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7r03l6f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
