\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Indonesian Interest Rate Decline Spooks Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2  By Grainne McCarthy \par \uc2 853 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1999\par 12:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's interest rate decline hit the rupiah Friday with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling to its lowest level in a month, prompting market participants to talk of an end to its long bull run. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's slide has also led to speculation that the downward trend in interest rates has come to an end. \par \par \uc2  With the Indonesian election commission expected to finally endorse the June poll results Monday and allocate parliamentary seats, concerns that Indonesia's political transition may not pass off peacefully are also weighing on the rupiah, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Market participants continue to gamble that Megawati Sukarnopurti's Indonesian Democratic Party of Struggle, or PDI-P, has the best chance of piecing together a coalition capable of winning the presidency later this year. \par \par \uc2  However, lingering signals that incumbent B.J. Habibie could also mount a challenge to retain the top job are causing some market jitters. \par \par \uc2  "People are a bit nervous," said Pardi Kendy, head of treasury at PT Bank Buana in Jakarta. "If PDI-P doesn't win, its supporters could go on the streets and create bloodshed." \par \par \uc2  The political concerns, coupled with external factors, including a general slump in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region and a hawkish interest rates stance by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan, all combined to pile pressure on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Having slipped slightly against the U.S. dollar over the past few\par days, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit an intraday low of IDR7,080 before ending Asian\par trade at IDR6,860 to the dollar, down 1.3% from late Thursday and the\par lowest level seen since June 22.\par          Interest Rate Decline Main Factor\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Jakarta Stock Market was also hit by the weaker rupiah and fears\par that the U.S. may raise rates at some point, sending the bellwether\par index down 2.6%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the main factor weighing on the rupiah, analysts say, is the\par decline in domestic short-term interest rates, which is causing the\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lose its attraction to investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Short-term rates have tumbled from their lofty highs of 70% last\par August to around 35% at the beginning of the year, and now stand at\par 14.5%. To a large extent, Bank Indonesia has managed to guide interest\par rates down to ease pressure on the real economy while not harming the\par rupiah, mainly by decoupling interest rates from the exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That policy worked effectively as long as rates remained sufficiently\par high by regional standards to still attract punters to the rupiah. Now,\par that perception has changed, prompting many in the market to gamble that\par the downward rate trend will stop at next week's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  paper\par auction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Bank Indonesia has to be very cautious in terms of lowering interest\par rates further," said Ruth Setyabandi, treasury chief at Chase Manhattan\par in Jakarta. "This is a very delicate balancing act for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The policy of allowing rates to fall at Bank Indonesia's weekly\par Sertifikat Bank Indonesia auction has also been effective as other\par positive factors were supporting the rupiah while rates were declining.\par          Greenspan Factor Weighs On Market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Signs that the pickup in other Asian economies has abated though,\par coupled with the tensions between China and Taiwan and the cloud of a\par U.S. interest rate hike hanging over the region, means those supporting\par factors are no longer there.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Greenspan and regional concerns are all fundamental reasons to\par weaken the rupiah," said Kevin Ng, economist at ABN Amro in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Money market participants in Jakarta say the rate decline already\par prompted some to avoid buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  notes at the auctions over\par the past couple of weeks and has led to large sales of SBI stocks in the\par secondary market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Rates are going lower and lower and people fear they could fall to\par single digits," said Pardi, at Bank Buana. "For those expecting high\par yield from the rupiah, there's no reason to buy it."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, the government and the International Monetary Fund said Friday\par that there was still room to "cautiously" let rates fall further. The\par IMF has said interest rates could fall to historic single digit lows by\par the end of the year, while Bank Indonesia says they would likely fall to\par between 10-14%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Given the regional downturn though, market participants doubt interest\par rates can continue to fall for now, particularly while Indonesia's\par political future remains uncertain.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, most dealers don't expect the rupiah to slide dramatically and\par many bulls still expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen back to IDR6,500 to\par the greenback by the end of the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Pardi noted that the presence of the state banks in the market Friday\par in bidding the rupiah back up was evidence that Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to halt any marked weakening in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I believe the market will try again to break the IDR7,000 level, but\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and government will do its utmost to stop that," he\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Grainne McCarthy; 6221 3983 1277; gmccarthy@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-07-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1036GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7n05j2b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
