\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Market Rates Dn; Liquidity Improves \b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 04:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money market rates are mostly lower early Wednesday as liquidity has improved after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released 2.607 trillion rupiah into the system. \par \par \uc2  The liquidity arises from the maturity of funds Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  absorbed in previous money market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0152 GMT (9:52 p.m. Tuesday EDT), the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was between 13.0% and 13.5%, down from between 13.5% and 14.0% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Later in the day, Bank Indonesia will auction one-month notes with the aim of absorbing IDR19 trillion from the market. The yield on the notes is expected to fall by up to 100 basis points from 15.86% last week. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at the same time, the dollar was trading at IDR6,693, little changed from IDR6,700 late Tuesday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana;(62-21) 3983 1277; imsentana@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0210GMT \par \par \uc2  1185 4281 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7l05exw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
