\par\par \b \uc2  FACTBOX - Chronology of financial crisis. \b0\par\par\uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 1999\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 28 (Reuters) - The following is a chronology of the financial crisis in emerging markets, first triggered by devaluation of the Thai baht two years ago. \par \par \uc2  1997 \par \par \uc2  July 2 - After a failed defence of the Thai baht, Bangkok floats its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and calls on the IMF for "technical assistance". The baht is effectively devalued by about 15-20 percent. \par \par \uc2  July 8 - Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara has to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to defend the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupiah starts to crumble. \par \par \uc2  July 14 - The IMF offers the Philippines almost $1.1 billion in financial support. \par \par \uc2  July 24 - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  meltdown. The rupiah, baht, ringgit and peso slump as confidence in the region deteriorates. \par \par \uc2  August 11 - In Tokyo, the IMF unveils a rescue package for Thailand including loans of $16 billion from the IMF and Asian nations. \par \par \uc2  August 14 - Indonesia abolishes its system of a managed exchange rate. The rupiah plunges. \par \par \uc2  Oct 20-23 - The Hong Kong stock market suffers its heaviest drubbing ever, shedding nearly a quarter of its value in four days on uncertainty over the Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  Oct 27 - Asian jitters spill over to world stock markets. The Dow plunges 554 points, its largest ever single-day point loss. \par \par \uc2  Oct 31 - IMF unveils Indonesia's $40 billion aid package, of which $23 billion is front-line defence. \par \par \uc2  Nov 17 - Korea abandons its defence of the won. \par \par \uc2  1998 \par \par \uc2  Jan 12 - Peregrine, one of Asia's largest independent investment banks, collapses under a mountain of bad loans to Indonesian borrowers. \par \par \uc2  Jan 22 - The rupiah collapses. It is dealt at 17,000 to the dollar at one stage. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  and drives the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to end at 11,800. \par \par \uc2  March 23 - Indonesia nearly doubles interest rates to boost the rupiah and control inflation. \par \par \uc2  May 21 - President Suharto of Indonesia steps down under strong pressure and is succeeded by former deputy president B.J. Habibie. \par \par \uc2  June 5 - International lenders and Indonesian companies reach a deal to reschedule the country's massive corporate debt. \par \par \uc2  June 10 - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor warns that the weak yen is having a severe impact on Beijing's foreign trade. \par \par \uc2  In Taiwan, the local dollar hits new 11-year lows and the Australian dollar plummets past 59 U.S. cents. \par \par \uc2  June 29 - South Korea closes banks for the first time, shutting five ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a major step towards meeting the mandate of the IMF rescue package. \par \par \uc2  July 13 - Japanese Prime Minister Hashimoto resigns. \par \par \uc2  August 17 - Russia sets a 90-day partial debt moratorium on foreign credits, says short-term rouble debt will be restructured. Government abandons floor value for rouble of 7.13 to the dollar, saying new lower limit is 9.5. \par \par \uc2  August 25 - Rouble suffers its worst one-day fall in nearly four years. Government announces rouble debt restructuring with terms which foreign investors say amount to default. \par \par \uc2  August 28 - Rouble trade is suspended indefinitely on the main Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange (MICEX). \par \par \uc2  August 31 - Wall Street suffers its second-largest points loss in history, plunging 6.37 percent and sparking another series of stock market routs in Asia. \par \par \uc2  September 2 - Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandons support for the rouble. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia announces that the ringgit will be fixed at 3.80 to the dollar indefinitely. \par \par \uc2  Wall Street stages its second-largest comeback in history, sparking a rally in Asian markets. \par \par \uc2  September 3 - Deputy Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim is sacked. \par \par \uc2  September 9 - Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Sergei Dubinin quits. \par \par \uc2  October 2 - Russian exporters start selling half of their hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues at MICEX under a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  order aimed at supporting the rouble. Shares hit all-time lows. \par \par \uc2  October 28 - Brazil unveils a 28 billion reals ($23.5 billion) austerity plan of budget cuts and tax hikes to shore up the economy. \par \par \uc2  November 6 - The Russian government and foreign banks agree in general on terms to restructure short-term rouble debt. \par \par \uc2  November 13 - The International Monetary Fund (IMF) and rich nations announce a loan package totalling more than $41 billion for Brazil to avoid a financial meltdown in Latin America. \par \par \uc2  1999 \par \par \uc2  January 13 - Brazil plunges deeper into crisis and sends world markets tumbling when it devalues the real. \par \par \uc2  June 15 - Mexico unveils a $23.7 billion financing programme designed to fireproof its economy. \par \par \uc2  March 10 - Brazil's lower house of parliament passes a bill raising a financial transaction tax, a key measure in its anti-crisis austerity plan. \par \par \uc2  April 28 - The IMF agrees to lend Russia $4.5 billion over 18 months but insists several reform proposals must be passed by its parliament before the money is released. \par \par \uc2  June 15 - Mexico unveils a $23.7 billion financing programme designed to fireproof its economy. \par \par \uc2  June 17 - Russia's State Duma votes against a petrol tax bill considered vital to win IMF cash promised in April. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6s05mj1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
