\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Mkt Rates Flat In Slow Afternoon Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 1999\par 11:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money market rates were flat\par Wednesday afternoon on abundant liquidity and lack of demand for\par funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0836 GMT (4:36 a.m. EDT), the overnight interbank rate - considered\par the benchmark rate - was between 24.5% and 25.0%, unchanged from\par Wednesday, for foreign banks and state banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Local banks of poorer quality were trading one to two percentage points higher. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was liquid and banks showed little incentive to open new positions ahead of the long weekend. Parliamentary elections will be held Monday, June 7. \par \par \uc2  "No one is brave enough to trade aggressively in the market," a dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  They said the market was flush with liquidity as Bank Indonesia released about IDR4.71 trillion into the money market earlier. \par \par \uc2  The amount came from the maturity of Bank Indonesia's short-term notes and the reversal of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market added another. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market daily to absorb excess liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "Banks want to wait and see what will happen to the election campaign and the election result," another dealer at an American bank said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to absorb excess liquidity in the market at 23%. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the rupiah has weakened slightly to trade at IDR8,200 to the dollar, compared with IDR8,160 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; 6221-3983-1277; nfung@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 03-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0902GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv63048n4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
