\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Mkt Rates Firm On Foreign Bk Fund Demand \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 1999\par 05:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money market rates were firm Tuesday morning as demand for funds from foreign banks kept rates high despite lower \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates set by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0243 GMT, the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was between 27% and 28% for foreign and joint venture banks, flat from Monday. Local banks, however, bid overnight for the rupiah between 30% and 31%, also unchanged from Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign banks are borrowing from the money market on the short end to fund their purchase of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-month notes. \par \par \uc2  "That's because banks are expecting interest rates to come down, that's the strategy to lock in profit," said a dealer at a British bank. \par \par \uc2  Banks buying the one-month notes can lock in the high interest rates while funding such purchases through the money market, where rates are falling. \par \par \uc2  Signaling its resolve to lower interest rates, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week cut its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates across the board - overnight rate to 25% from 27%; the two- through six-day rates to 28.5% from 30%; and the one-week rate to 29.5% from 31.0%. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market daily to absorb excess liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect to see another 100- to 200-basis-point fall in Wednesday's auction of one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes. \par \par \uc2  The government has repeatedly expressed its wish to see interest rates fall to single-digit levels by the end of the fiscal year in March next year. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes yielded 31.47%, lower from 33.21% a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the rupiah maintained its strength and was quoted at IDR7,625 to the dollar at 0301 GMT, stronger than IDR7,850 traded late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Noel Fung; 6221-3983-1277; nfung@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-05-99 \par \par \uc2  0330GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5b03jo7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
