\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Market Rates Flat On Ample Liquidity \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 1999\par 05:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money market rates were mostly flat early Tuesday as liquidity remained flush and the market's attention focused on the weekly auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes. \par \par \uc2  At 0304 GMT (10:04 p.m. Monday EDT), the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was between 30.5% to 31.5% among foreign banks and good joint-venture banks, flat from Monday. \par \par \uc2  The second tier banks, comprising primarily of state-owned banks and joint-venture banks, were trading at 32% to 34% for overnight funds, unchanged from the day before. \par \par \uc2  Local banks obtained overnight rupiah funds at around 35%. \par \par \uc2  Taking the cue from Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  which left its overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate unchanged at 30%, dealers said the money market rates stayed at similar levels compared to Monday. \par \par \uc2  Abundant liquidity has kept money market rates soft, they said. \par \par \uc2  The market is focusing on the weekly auction of the one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes rate fell by 82 basis points. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at the same time, the dollar was trading at 8,600 rupiah (IDR) to the dollar, a touch stronger from IDR8,650 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-04-99 \par \par \uc2  0340GMT \par \par \uc2  1185 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4k03286\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\