\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Market Down Early After End Of Fiscal Year \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 1999\par 05:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money market rates were mostly lower early Monday as demand for rupiah subsided after the end of the fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  Demand for rupiah increased sharply last week as companies paid taxes for the 1998/1999 fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  At 0241 GMT (10:41 p.m. Sunday EDT), the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was at 31% for foreign banks, down from 34% Thursday. The market was closed Friday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate for state-banks was between 32% and 33%, down from 34% Thursday; between 37% and 39% for healthy private local banks, down from 40%; and 40% for local private banks which will be recapitalized, down from 45%. \par \par \uc2  "It seems liquidity is returning to the system as companies and depositors are putting their money in banks," said a dealer with a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Bank Indonesia injected 3.458 trillion rupiah (IDR) into the money market. The injection represents the reversal of previous Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  which absorbed excess liquidity through borrowing on maturities ranging from overnight to seven days. \par \par \uc2  In its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the overnight interest rate at 30%; two, three, and four day rates at 33%; and the one-week rate at 34%. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at 0241 GMT, the dollar was trading at IDR8,675, slightly up from IDR8,650 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana (62-2