\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals buoyed by firmer yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      1010 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were broadly firmer as \par \par \uc2  the yen strengthened on profit-taking by foreign funds which \par \par \uc2  had bought dollars on expectations of strong dollar demand. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said exporter offers were also depressing the \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2      But they said the dollar's downside was being supported so \par \par \uc2  far, as firm buying offers were said to be lined up at around \par \par \uc2  119.60-119.80 yen by Japanese investors. \par \par \uc2      *** Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bank Negara delivered a \par \par \uc2  cautiously upbeat outlook for 1999 in its annual report, \par \par \uc2  predicting the economy would recover modestly this year from \par \par \uc2  Asia's financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara said the country's gross domestic product was \par \par \uc2  expected to rise by one percent year-on-year in 1999 after \par \par \uc2  shrinking 6.7 percent the year before - its worst economic \par \par \uc2  performance since 1985. \par \par \uc2  It said the current account surplus was likely to shrink to \par \par \uc2  29.5 billion ringgit this year against 36.1 billion ringgit in \par \par \uc2  1998. \par \par \uc2      The Consumer Price Index is expected to be at four percent \par \par \uc2  against a 5.3 percent rise last year. \par \par \uc2      Bank Negara said interest rates would be maintained at \par \par \uc2  current levels if there were no inflationary pressures, which \par \par \uc2  it said was unlikely to be a serious risk. \par \par \uc2      *** The baht was again treading water after failing to \par \par \uc2  react to details of a $3.5 billion economic stimulus package, \par \par \uc2  unveiled by the government on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda said the package \par \par \uc2  should stimulate demand and help the economy grow between 0.4 \par \par \uc2  percent and 1.4 percent, depending on exports. \par \par \uc2      Thailand officially signed sale contracts with eight \par \par \uc2  companies that won bids in the country's recent auction of loan \par \par \uc2  assets seized from defunct finance companies. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won slipped as state-run banks absorbed \par \par \uc2  dollar offers from exporters. \par \par \uc2      The government said consumer prices fell sharply in March, \par \par \uc2  as the more stable won kept a lid on price rises. \par \par \uc2      The CPI rose 0.5 percent year-on-year, down from a massive \par \par \uc2  9.0 percent rise a year earlier. The PPI fell 4.3 percent \par \par \uc2  year-on-year in March, against a 15.1 percent rise a year ago. \par \par \uc2      The government said the trade surplus was expected to reach \par \par \uc2  $2.2 billion in March, compared with a $3.68 billion surplus \par \par \uc2  last year. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah was on the right side of 9,000 per dollar \par \par \uc2  amid speculation Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to \par \par \uc2  prop it up ahead of the fiscal year-end today. \par \par \uc2      The market failed to react to Standard & Poor's reversal of \par \par \uc2  a move on Tuesday to downgrade Indonesia's long-term foreign \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating. \par \par \uc2      S&P reset Indonesia's rating at triple-'C'-plus from SD \par \par \uc2  (selective default) and raised its outlook, ironically placing \par \par \uc2  Jakarta's rating higher than where it started the week. \par \par \uc2  It said the decision reflected Indonesia's rescheduling of \par \par \uc2  US$210 million worth of principal on a $350 million commercial \par \par \uc2  loan. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Miranda Goeltom said there \par \par \uc2  was a high chance the country would achieve its March target of \par \par \uc2  zero percent month-on-month inflation. \par \par \uc2  Month-on-month inflation fell to 1.26 percent in February \par \par \uc2  from 2.97 percent a month ago. The February consumer price \par \par \uc2  index stood at 207.12, 53.39 percent higher than in February \par \par \uc2  1998. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day WED 31 0932GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8650.00......8710.00.........0.69% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.60........37.66.........0.16% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.75........38.70........-0.13% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7285.......1.7330.........0.26% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...33.110.......33.120.........0.03% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1226.00......1223.50........-0.20% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....119.38.......120.11.........0.61% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest.....July '97.......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8650.00......2432.00........-71.88% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.60........25.90........-31.12% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.75........26.50........-31.61% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7285.......1.4300........-17.27% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..33.1100......27.7500........-16.19% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1226.00......