\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals languish with yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 03:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0055 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were narrowly tracking \par \par \uc2  the yen amid expectations of commercial dollar demand on the \par \par \uc2  last day of Japan's fiscal year. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the dollar should find firm support around \par \par \uc2  119.50 yen, while its advance would be limited to 121.50, where \par \par \uc2  exporter sales were expected. \par \par \uc2      They said Japanese banks were also expected to sell the yen \par \par \uc2  against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the euro and Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2      But the underlying trend of the euro remained bearish, \par \par \uc2  especially after the European Commission trimmed its 1999 \par \par \uc2  growth forecast to 2.2 percent from 2.6 percent. \par \par \uc2      The continuing Kosovo crisis also added pressure on the \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *** The IMF approved a $4.9 billion payment for Brazil, the \par \par \uc2  second installment of a massive international rescue deal \par \par \uc2  agreed last year. \par \par \uc2      *** The baht was again treading water after failing to \par \par \uc2  react to details of a $3.5 billion economic stimulus package, \par \par \uc2  unveiled by the government on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      The package aims to create almost half a million new jobs \par \par \uc2  through billions of baht in new government spending, tax breaks \par \par \uc2  for businesses and households and big cuts in energy prices. \par \par \uc2      Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda said the package \par \par \uc2  should stimulate demand and help the economy grow between 0.4 \par \par \uc2  percent and 1.4 percent, depending on exports. \par \par \uc2      The IMF gave a thumbs-up to the package, saying it was an \par \par \uc2  important step towards recovery, with tax cuts carefully \par \par \uc2  designed to boost consumer spending and lower costs. \par \par \uc2      But analysts said the measures were only likely to produce \par \par \uc2  results around the last quarter of this year as the proposed \par \par \uc2  government expenditure filtered through the economy. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won was steady after gaining a bit of ground \par \par \uc2  on Tuesday as exporters flooded the market with dollars. \par \par \uc2      The government said foreign direct investment plans \par \par \uc2  totalled $620 million in March, against $243 million a year \par \par \uc2  ago. \par \par \uc2      Commerce Minister Park Tae-young said FDI plans received in \par \par \uc2  the first quarter of this year totalled $1.9 billion from $572 \par \par \uc2  million the year before. \par \par \uc2      Park also said the government was considering easing the \par \par \uc2  strict 200 percent debt-to-equity ratio for major companies to \par \par \uc2  boost exports. \par \par \uc2      All companies are currently required to meet this target by \par \par \uc2  the end of the year. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah was holding up on the right side of 9,000 \par \par \uc2  per dollar amid speculation Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  aggressively to prop it up ahead of the fiscal year-end today. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the move was expected to help companies book \par \par \uc2  improved first quarter financial results. \par \par \uc2      It also helped to counter the impact of a ratings downgrade \par \par \uc2  by Standard & Poor's. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it regretted S&P's decision to slap \par \par \uc2  Indonesia with a "selective default" rating, noting that it had \par \par \uc2  never defaulted on commercial bank loans or bonds. \par \par \uc2      But an S&P official in New York said overnight that the \par \par \uc2  agency would probably remove the "selective default" foreign \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating before too long. \par \par \uc2      He said Indonesia's weekend move to restructure some of its \par \par \uc2  debt could be seen as creditor positive in the larger scheme of \par \par \uc2  things. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day WED 31 0057GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7999.......3.8000.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8725.00......8710.00........-0.17% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.70........37.66........-0.11% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.70........38.70.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7318.......1.7330.........0.07% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...33.120.......33.120.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1224.00......1223.50........-0.04% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....120.30.......120.11........-0.16% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7999.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8725.00......2432.00........-72.13% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........37.70........25.90........-31.30% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.70........26.50........-31.52% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7318.......1.4300........-17.43% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..33.1200......27.7500........-16.21% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1224.00.......842.00........-31.21% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen..