\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Money Mkt Rates Steady; No Bank-Deposit Runs Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 04:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesian money-market rates were mostly steady midmorning Monday, as the market digested the government's major bank-reform plans unveiled this weekend. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no evidence of deposit runs on banks in the wake of bank closures. \par \par \uc2  At 0320 GMT (10:20 p.m. Sunday EST), the overnight interbank rate - considered the benchmark rate - was between 32% and 33% for foreign and large joint-venture banks, unchanged from Friday. \par \par \uc2  "It's pretty much status quo in the money market," said the head of treasury at a foreign bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "You have to be positive," he said. "We've got through this weekend with a decent list of banks to close. It probably looked so bad two weeks ago, the market should be encouraged by this." \par \par \uc2  Indonesia closed 38 banks Saturday, took over seven others and said it would recapitalize an additional nine. The number of banks closed was at the top end of market expectations. \par \par \uc2  Treasury dealers said there was no evidence in the money market of deposit runs sparked by the closures - something which would become quickly evident from money-market liquidity movements. The treasury chief said this was because of the well-publicized fact that the government is guaranteeing all deposits. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the money market at a bidding rate of 33%, in a continued effort to drive the rupiah higher and absorb rupiah liquidity. \par \par \uc2  "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 33%," said a treasury dealer at a U.S. bank. "This is a good move. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to see the rupiah stronger and is trying to tighten rupiah liquidity." \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's early - relatively high - \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is unchanged from last week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected IDR5.732 trillion into the money market early Monday, as a result of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past week to absorb excess liquidity. \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets meanwhile, the rupiah was quoted at IDR8,930, stronger than IDR9,150 late Friday, as the market welcomed the banking announcement. \par \par \uc2  -By Grainne McCarthy; 6221 3983 1277; gmccarthy@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-03-99 \par \par \uc2  0357GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3f01z3b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
